Z||000018||Ken Wittlief||05-18-2001||11:21 AM||||when I first heard of the 'razzel-dazzel' paint schemes that were used on destroyers to confuse german U-boats, I thought it would be cool to do a car like that.<P>  the surface is painted with bright yellow and orange and red areas and shapes, with jagged diagonal black lines and sharp points everywhere. it confused the sub cause when you saw the ship, it wasnt camoflogged, but you couldnt tell what the H#LL you were looking at, what class of ship it was, what dierction it was pointed.<P><BR>   But the drawback is the car would be an accident magnet.||||reg||1
